<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Salapify keeps a person's whole ledger, their salary, their debts and the
    names of people who owe them money, in one JSON file in the app's own
    documents directory. Two rules below, and they are deliberately different
    from each other.

    CLOUD BACKUP IS OFF. A copy of that file in Google Drive is a copy Salapify
    cannot see, cannot check and cannot delete when somebody asks us to delete
    their data. android:allowBackup="false" in the manifest already turns it
    off; this file says so again where a reader will look for it, and is what
    actually governs it from Android 12 onward.

    DEVICE TO DEVICE TRANSFER IS ON, and that is the part worth explaining.
    D2D copies straight from the old phone to the new one during setup, with no
    server anywhere in the path, while the person is holding both handsets. That
    is somebody moving their own data across, not a silent upload, so it stays.

    WHERE THE LEDGER ACTUALLY IS. Until 2026-10-09 this file included only the
    "file" domain, which is the app's files/ folder, and the ledger is not
    there. path_provider's getApplicationDocumentsDirectory on Android is
    Context.getDir("flutter"), which is the folder app_flutter/ beside files/,
    not inside it. So the transfer described above copied nothing of the
    money while the privacy sheet promised it did. The "root" rule below is
    what reaches app_flutter/ (the ledger, its safety copies, the Pan
    conversation and the rate cache). It is the ONLY include: the old
    "file" rule reached nothing Salapify writes, and left in place it would
    have quietly carried whatever a future plugin kept in files/.

    APP LOCK STAYS BEHIND, by founder decision ("keep it out"). app_lock.json
    and its half-written .tmp are excluded, so the new phone opens unlocked
    and the person turns the lock on again there, against that phone's own
    screen lock. test/data/data_transfer_rules_test.dart holds both rules.

    THIS IS NOT THE USER'S BACKUP. Their backup is the export they are owed and
    do not have yet. Do not let this file be mistaken for having built it.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="file" />
        <exclude domain="database" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
        <exclude domain="external" />
        <exclude domain="device_root" />
        <exclude domain="device_file" />
        <exclude domain="device_database" />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="root" path="app_flutter/" />
        <exclude domain="root" path="app_flutter/app_lock.json" />
        <exclude domain="root" path="app_flutter/app_lock.json.tmp" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
